WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.220
So, how do we take this M.V.P. Blueprint from a document into your playbook and make it

00:06.220 --> 00:10.680
living, breathing, a part of your leadership operating system?

00:10.680 --> 00:14.860
You start by using it as a decision filter.

00:14.860 --> 00:20.100
Every day, you're faced with a dozen choices.

00:20.100 --> 00:25.420
Without a clear filter, you often make these choices based on what's the loudest, what's

00:25.420 --> 00:30.380
the most urgent, or what we think others expect of us.

00:30.380 --> 00:34.860
This is a recipe for burnout and reactive leadership.

00:34.860 --> 00:39.940
As athletes, using your M.V.P. is a strategic filter.

00:39.940 --> 00:41.780
Let me give you a real example.

00:41.780 --> 00:47.740
I coached a director, let's call her Anna, whose purpose statement was to champion emerging

00:47.740 --> 00:51.580
talent and build the next generation of leaders.

00:51.580 --> 00:56.860
Her mission was to dedicate her time to mentorship and creating growth opportunities for her

00:56.860 --> 00:58.340
team.

00:58.340 --> 01:04.300
One afternoon, her boss offered her a stretch assignment, a high-profile project analyzing

01:04.300 --> 01:06.100
market data.

01:06.100 --> 01:11.940
But it was solitary work that would take her away from her team a full quarter.

01:11.940 --> 01:19.820
A year ago, she would have said yes instantly, but now she ran it through her M.V.P. filter.

01:19.820 --> 01:25.100
She asked, does this project align with my purpose of championing talent?

01:25.100 --> 01:28.300
Does it support my mission of mentoring my team?

01:28.300 --> 01:31.220
The answer was a clear no.

01:31.220 --> 01:36.420
So she went back to her boss and said, listen, I'm honored by the offer.

01:36.420 --> 01:38.220
It's a critical project.

01:38.220 --> 01:44.780
However, my core focus this quarter, as we discussed, is on developing my team to increase

01:44.780 --> 01:47.100
our overall capacity.

01:47.100 --> 01:50.020
Should we delegate this to my rising star, David?

01:50.020 --> 01:55.140
I will oversee it, and I will make sure that it will be a fantastic growth opportunity

01:55.140 --> 01:56.140
for him.

01:56.140 --> 01:57.140
Hmm.

01:57.140 --> 01:58.700
Do you see what happened?

01:58.700 --> 02:00.180
She didn't just say no.

02:00.180 --> 02:04.340
She used her M.V.P. to propose a powerful yes.

02:04.340 --> 02:09.180
She stayed true to her purpose, created a growth opportunity for her direct report,

02:09.180 --> 02:13.260
and demonstrated strategic leadership to her boss.

02:13.260 --> 02:17.220
This is activating your M.V.P. in your playbook.

02:17.220 --> 02:22.780
You'll work through a scenario to practice using your own M.V.P. as a decision filter.

